Ai:
Before launching the AI model, the authority should use the NIST AI Risk Management Framework (AI RMF) to manage key risks. These include false alerts, breaches of attack, unfair decision, privacy breach, and security threat. The accuracy, fairness and reliability of the model should be tested. The authority should also track its performance, secure the citizens' data, and give its staff access to suspicious log-in alerts.
Resource: NIST AI Risk Management Framework - https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-981-95-3658-0_57 

mobile:
The runtime permission model is a model implemented by Android that restricts access to sensitive information and phone features to apps. The login app requires the necessary permission in order to be able to access protected data, such as contacts or location. It should request permission and access to the user when a feature requires access and hasn't been requested previously. The app should provide a reason for the access and if the access is denied, the app should continue functioning if possible. The article also cautions that some permissions could be granted without re-prompting.
resource: Android Developers – Request runtime permissions. - https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27667 
